#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415480} :activity/id #uuid "d3285aa6-5f09-548a-886c-a1acc2f7b8d6" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415480 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} {:answer/id #uuid "68acb0f6-b335-5e47-b870-8fcc301ed02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415455} {:answer/id #uuid "a31adf10-60d1-51b5-9022-8cf1940c42be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415461} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaffa84-7e8a-5edc-8432-6adf9e5b2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415465} {:answer/id #uuid "fae22a7a-c8b8-5a0b-bb2c-5bc815b3b48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ec239f-8a57-5ead-b4ff-042aa539477e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d4554f29-f5fb-5556-852c-2f9d95422a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42464" :question/problem "Find $5det(A)+7det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+7det(B)=5\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0=0.$"} :step/id #uuid "0922e6fb-1dc5-5a88-a985-bdf2643cb465" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415484}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415481 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d00532a-c12b-50b9-ad0b-b9f1fa474794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415449} {:answer/id #uuid "44173bde-0fab-57de-b1b3-22d94262de8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415452} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9c1118-9a19-54c3-9683-cf1248dd342b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415456} {:answer/id #uuid "7e862f84-0fe3-5f4e-8829-b54fb65649ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415457} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd19d7-7290-5199-aa60-b1bc0b2d73b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80361a1-690f-54bf-a979-055f8bec64f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has two proportional rows\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} :step/id #uuid "73a434b3-1e72-5102-a3b4-f3e485e5088a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415482}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415482 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045918a8-9cd8-5a07-b550-ae46024d9091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415446} {:answer/id #uuid "402ee237-56af-5ed0-b68b-15a4eb93a4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415451} {:answer/id #uuid "82c9a685-f3be-5652-9e92-444a23e21632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415458} {:answer/id #uuid "f5705fa2-288d-561a-9ae0-435e05884593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} {:answer/id #uuid "fff98d8e-e1e9-59ce-9f45-62d4096f2b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415469}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898e8c8-305f-5107-8e55-3fa0057b225c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "135c5d03-e391-5a5b-8227-7d54c7203318" :question/math-academy-id "q-140048" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n|A|=0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0=0\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "7fde0eea-1a95-5e36-bc1d-53171442da99"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415483 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1859d7c5-0d55-5273-a004-f8368886466b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415448} {:answer/id #uuid "4a61a420-d52d-5f1a-b48b-ade03dffdca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415453} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcc61bd-b9ee-5f9e-8558-651f8ea9c858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415454} {:answer/id #uuid "851dc3ec-467b-568b-a964-3b5e34b3527e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415459} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4e722-717d-508c-a98d-112f70b09d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463} :answer-field/id #uuid "f920ea7f-06a7-52e9-8586-d0e6b44af6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e897ce2c-45dd-5cf3-9d25-ca84c0dd6ea8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42881" :question/problem "Find $3det(A)-det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-det(B)=3\\cdot 6-0=18.$"} :step/id #uuid "8a73fe86-1dcc-5158-b5d0-cfa5bf0ca01e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415481}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415484 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143f48c0-a939-5a4c-b987-afdbbefec79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415447} {:answer/id #uuid "22066df8-6293-5194-a873-db4b694c6674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415450} {:answer/id #uuid "8e60b08a-cd17-575f-8815-735e23870208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415460} {:answer/id #uuid "b446fc5b-8c89-5d67-acf5-bbcf1be8249d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415462} {:answer/id #uuid "fe594f39-ea49-5697-a493-c1ebeaf625b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415468}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415450} :answer-field/id #uuid "44a7cadd-9704-50b9-80ee-df6bc66a727b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8d883981-f066-5218-a1bf-dd76574de46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42469" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has identical rows\n- $A$ has a zero row" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "a995ede1-d1f3-53d5-97cb-aed29dce50f7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415483}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415444}]}
